# Nav graphs are gzipped ds_grid_write blobs. Even uncompressed they are a
# single multi-megabyte line of hex, so there has never been anything here for
# git to diff or three-way merge — a conflict in one is not resolvable by hand
# and must not look as though it is. gg2-nav-gen regenerates them wholesale;
# that is the merge strategy. See NavCache and docs/DEPLOY.md.
nav/*.txt      binary
nav/*.txt.gz   binary

# ...but the manifest beside them is the human-readable half and stays diffable:
# its diff is how you see WHICH map's geometry moved. NavManifestTests.
nav/manifest.tsv   text eol=lf

# Map PNGs carry their level data in a zTXt chunk. Git detects them as binary
# anyway; saying so keeps a mis-set core.autocrlf from corrupting one.
maps/*.png     binary

# The recorded traces and fixture blobs are compared byte-for-byte against the
# running game and against numpy oracles, so a line-ending rewrite is a silent
# fixture change. docs/PARITY.md.
*.trace        binary
*.bin          binary
*.npz          binary

# Shell scripts are read by bash, and a CR at the end of every line is a syntax
# error there rather than a cosmetic difference. core.autocrlf=true would put one
# on every line at checkout, so the ending is pinned here instead of left to a
# machine's configuration - scripts/deploy.sh also pipes its remote half through
# `ssh host bash -s`, where the same CRs would arrive at a Linux shell.
*.sh           text eol=lf

# MaxMind DB fixtures are the geo reader's own oracle, built by the format's
# authors and read byte-for-byte. Git detects them as binary anyway; saying so
# keeps a mis-set core.autocrlf from corrupting one, as for the maps above.
*.mmdb         binary
